# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Model weights (baked into the Docker image at build time; don't commit)
*.onnx
*.bin

# Generated audio / cache
*.wav
tts-cache/

# Env / editor / OS
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Knowledge base artifacts.
#
# The corpus is the scrape output and IS committed: it takes ~40 minutes to
# regenerate against the live site.
#
# The *index* is now committed too, which it did not used to be. Embeddings were
# a local ONNX model, so the Docker build could rebuild the index for free; they
# are a metered Gemini call now, so rebuilding at image-build time would need a
# live key, spend quota, and could fail on a 429 — for an artifact that only
# changes when the corpus does. Build it locally with `python -m kb.index` and
# commit the result; the image just uses it.
kb-data/*
!kb-data/corpus.jsonl
!kb-data/chunks.jsonl
!kb-data/vectors.npy
!kb-data/index-meta.json

# Derived caches: rebuilt on demand, machine-specific, and large.
# embed-cache.jsonl makes a re-index incremental (only changed chunks are sent
# to the API) but it is reproducible, so it stays out of the repo.
kb-data/embed-cache.jsonl
kb-data/answer-cache*.jsonl
kb-data/html-cache/
kb-data/quarantine.jsonl
kb-data/corpus.before.jsonl
models/

debug.log